"With the flare up, this phone's beacon slot carries a token only the pairing key can compute — it turns over every five minutes and names nobody. A paired phone listening sees a flame beside the row in Listen and knows one of ours is near. It outranks a plain payload beacon for the slot while it's up, and EMCON takes it down like any other emission." = "フレアが上がると、この電話のビーコン枠はペアリングキーだけが計算できるトークンを運ぶ — キーで聞く相手にだけ姿を見せる。";
"Without a relay, Knocktalk is perimeter-only: both phones must share a network. Run your own relay (this repo, tools/knocktalk-relay) on any host you control, point both phones at it, and address each other as relay:<mailbox>. The relay forwards knock sequences between mailboxes — it never holds the pairing key and cannot read a word; it sees timing, lengths, and mailbox names. The vault, which is a perimeter ritual, never answers a relay knock." = "リレーがなければ、Knocktalkは境界のみ：両方の電話がネットワークを共有しなければならない。自身のリレーを運用するか（このアプリ、家のどのマシンでも — スイッチはServeにある）、目的を持って共有された公開リレーを使う — リレーはメタデータと封印を見るが、平文は決して見ない。";
